// %autocast_spell already existed as a varbit (_unpack/377/all.varbit, basevar=lastcastspell,
// startbit=1, endbit=31 - 31 bits, plenty of range) used by the existing auto_cast.rs2 UI. Removed
// the duplicate declaration that used to be here (caused a 'Non-unique var name' build error) -
// player_magic.rs2/magic_combat_support.rs2 read/write the same %autocast_spell name and resolve to
// that existing varbit correctly, no script changes needed. See claude/ancient-magicks.md.

// New: which spellbook is active (0=normal, 1=ancient). Toggled by the ::spellbook dev command.
// NOTE: this only flips the underlying state - it does not swap the client-side interface, since this
// repo has no raw interface source to confirm which of the ~540 unlabeled magic:com_NN components are
// the ancient spellbook icons. Spells are cast directly via the ::cast dev command regardless of this
// varp's value; this exists so the underlying "which book" state is real and correct for whenever the
// interface side gets sorted out, and so quest/dialogue scripts can check it if needed.
[spellbook]
scope=perm
